---DescribeTaskExecutionRequest
---@class aws.datasync.DescribeTaskExecutionRequest
---@field TaskExecutionArn aws.datasync.TaskExecutionArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the task execution that you want information about.

---DescribeTaskExecutionResponse
---@class aws.datasync.DescribeTaskExecutionResponse
---@field TaskExecutionArn? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionArn The ARN of the task execution that you wanted information about. TaskExecutionArn is hierarchical and includes TaskArn for the task that was executed.
---@field Status? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionStatus The status of the task execution.
---@field Options? aws.datasync.OptionsShape
---@field Excludes? aws.datasync.FilterList A list of filter rules that exclude specific data during your transfer. For more information and examples, see Filtering data transferred by DataSync.
---@field Includes? aws.datasync.FilterList A list of filter rules that include specific data during your transfer. For more information and examples, see Filtering data transferred by DataSync.
---@field ManifestConfig? aws.datasync.ManifestConfig The configuration of the manifest that lists the files or objects to transfer. For more information, see Specifying what DataSync transfers by using a manifest.
---@field StartTime? aws.datasync.Time The time that DataSync sends the request to start the task execution. For non-queued tasks, LaunchTime and StartTime are typically the same. For queued tasks, LaunchTime is typically later than StartTime because previously queued tasks must finish running before newer tasks can begin.
---@field EstimatedFilesToTransfer aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync expects to transfer over the network. This value is calculated while DataSync prepares the transfer.
---@field EstimatedBytesToTransfer aws.datasync.long The number of logical bytes that DataSync expects to write to the destination location.
---@field FilesTransferred aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync actually transfers over the network. This value is updated periodically during your task execution when something is read from the source and sent over the network.
---@field BytesWritten aws.datasync.long The number of logical bytes that DataSync actually writes to the destination location.
---@field BytesTransferred aws.datasync.long The number of bytes that DataSync sends to the network before compression (if compression is possible). For the number of bytes transferred over the network, see BytesCompressed.
---@field BytesCompressed aws.datasync.long The number of physical bytes that DataSync transfers over the network after compression (if compression is possible). This number is typically less than BytesTransferred unless the data isn't compressible.
---@field Result? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionResultDetail The result of the task execution.
---@field TaskReportConfig? aws.datasync.TaskReportConfig The configuration of your task report, which provides detailed information about for your DataSync transfer. For more information, see Creating a task report.
---@field FilesDeleted aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync actually deletes in your destination location. If you don't configure your task to delete data in the destination that isn't in the source, the value is always 0.
---@field FilesSkipped aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync skips during your transfer.
---@field FilesVerified aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync verifies during your transfer.
---@field ReportResult? aws.datasync.ReportResult Indicates whether DataSync generated a complete task report for your transfer.
---@field EstimatedFilesToDelete aws.datasync.long The number of files, objects, and directories that DataSync expects to delete in your destination location. If you don't configure your task to delete data in the destination that isn't in the source, the value is always 0.
---@field TaskMode? aws.datasync.TaskMode The task mode that you're using. For more information, see Choosing a task mode for your data transfer.
---@field FilesPrepared aws.datasync.long The number of files or objects that DataSync will attempt to transfer after comparing your source and destination locations.
---@field FilesListed? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionFilesListedDetail The number of files or objects that DataSync finds at your locations.
---@field FilesFailed? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionFilesFailedDetail The number of files or objects that DataSync fails to prepare, transfer, verify, and delete during your task execution.
---@field EstimatedFoldersToDelete? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync expects to delete in your destination location. If you don't configure your task to delete data in the destination that isn't in the source, the value is always 0.
---@field EstimatedFoldersToTransfer? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync expects to transfer over the network. This value is calculated as DataSync prepares directories to transfer.
---@field FoldersSkipped? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync skips during your transfer.
---@field FoldersPrepared? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync will attempt to transfer after comparing your source and destination locations.
---@field FoldersTransferred? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync actually transfers over the network. This value is updated periodically during your task execution when something is read from the source and sent over the network.
---@field FoldersVerified? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync verifies during your transfer.
---@field FoldersDeleted? aws.datasync.ItemCount The number of directories that DataSync actually deletes in your destination location. If you don't configure your task to delete data in the destination that isn't in the source, the value is always 0.
---@field FoldersListed? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionFoldersListedDetail The number of directories that DataSync finds at your locations.
---@field FoldersFailed? aws.datasync.TaskExecutionFoldersFailedDetail The number of directories that DataSync fails to list, prepare, transfer, verify, and delete during your task execution.
---@field LaunchTime? aws.datasync.Time The time that the task execution actually begins. For non-queued tasks, LaunchTime and StartTime are typically the same. For queued tasks, LaunchTime is typically later than StartTime because previously queued tasks must finish running before newer tasks can begin.
---@field EndTime? aws.datasync.Time The time that the transfer task ends.

