---@field DestinationNetworkInterfaceArns? aws.datasync.DestinationNetworkInterfaceArns The ARNs of the network interfaces that DataSync created for your destination location.
---@field Options? aws.datasync.OptionsShape The task's settings. For example, what file metadata gets preserved, how data integrity gets verified at the end of your transfer, bandwidth limits, among other options.
---@field Excludes? aws.datasync.FilterList The exclude filters that define the files, objects, and folders in your source location that you don't want DataSync to transfer. For more information and examples, see Specifying what DataSync transfers by using filters.
---@field Schedule? aws.datasync.TaskSchedule The schedule for when you want your task to run. For more information, see Scheduling your task.
---@field ErrorCode? aws.datasync.string If there's an issue with your task, you can use the error code to help you troubleshoot the problem. For more information, see Troubleshooting issues with DataSync transfers.
---@field ErrorDetail? aws.datasync.string If there's an issue with your task, you can use the error details to help you troubleshoot the problem. For more information, see Troubleshooting issues with DataSync transfers.
---@field CreationTime? aws.datasync.Time The time that the task was created.
---@field Includes? aws.datasync.FilterList The include filters that define the files, objects, and folders in your source location that you want DataSync to transfer. For more information and examples, see Specifying what DataSync transfers by using filters.
---@field ManifestConfig? aws.datasync.ManifestConfig The configuration of the manifest that lists the files or objects that you want DataSync to transfer. For more information, see Specifying what DataSync transfers by using a manifest.
---@field TaskReportConfig? aws.datasync.TaskReportConfig The configuration of your task report, which provides detailed information about your DataSync transfer. For more information, see Monitoring your DataSync transfers with task reports.
---@field ScheduleDetails? aws.datasync.TaskScheduleDetails The details about your task schedule.
---@field TaskMode? aws.datasync.TaskMode The task mode that you're using. For more information, see Choosing a task mode for your data transfer.

