---Indicates how your transfer task is configured. These options include how DataSync handles files, objects, and their associated metadata during your transfer. You also can specify how to verify data integrity, set bandwidth limits for your task, among other options.
---@class aws.datasync.OptionsShape
---@field VerifyMode? aws.datasync.VerifyMode|string Specifies if and how DataSync checks the integrity of your data at the end of your transfer.
---@field OverwriteMode? aws.datasync.OverwriteMode|string Specifies whether DataSync should modify or preserve data at the destination location.
---@field Atime? aws.datasync.Atime|string Specifies whether to preserve metadata indicating the last time a file was read or written to.
---@field Mtime? aws.datasync.Mtime|string Specifies whether to preserve metadata indicating the last time that a file was written to before the PREPARING step of your task execution. This option is required when you need to run the a task more than once.
---@field Uid? aws.datasync.Uid|string Specifies the POSIX user ID (UID) of the file's owner.
---@field Gid? aws.datasync.Gid|string Specifies the POSIX group ID (GID) of the file's owners.
---@field PreserveDeletedFiles? aws.datasync.PreserveDeletedFiles|string Specifies whether files in the destination location that don't exist in the source should be preserved. This option can affect your Amazon S3 storage cost. If your task deletes objects, you might incur minimum storage duration charges for certain storage classes. For detailed information, see Considerations when working with Amazon S3 storage classes in DataSync.
---@field PreserveDevices? aws.datasync.PreserveDevices|string Specifies whether DataSync should preserve the metadata of block and character devices in the source location and recreate the files with that device name and metadata on the destination. DataSync copies only the name and metadata of such devices.
---@field PosixPermissions? aws.datasync.PosixPermissions|string Specifies which users or groups can access a file for a specific purpose such as reading, writing, or execution of the file.
---@field BytesPerSecond? aws.datasync.BytesPerSecond Limits the bandwidth used by a DataSync task. For example, if you want DataSync to use a maximum of 1 MB, set this value to 1048576 (=1024*1024).
---@field TaskQueueing? aws.datasync.TaskQueueing|string Specifies whether your transfer tasks should be put into a queue during certain scenarios when running multiple tasks. This is ENABLED by default.
---@field LogLevel? aws.datasync.LogLevel|string Specifies the type of logs that DataSync publishes to a Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. To specify the log group, see CloudWatchLogGroupArn.
---@field TransferMode? aws.datasync.TransferMode|string Specifies whether DataSync transfers only the data (including metadata) that differs between locations following an initial copy or transfers all data every time you run the task. If you're planning on recurring transfers, you might only want to transfer what's changed since your previous task execution.
---@field SecurityDescriptorCopyFlags? aws.datasync.SmbSecurityDescriptorCopyFlags|string Specifies which components of the SMB security descriptor are copied from source to destination objects.
---@field ObjectTags? aws.datasync.ObjectTags|string Specifies whether you want DataSync to PRESERVE object tags (default behavior) when transferring between object storage systems. If you want your DataSync task to ignore object tags, specify the NONE value.
---@field ObjectMetadata? aws.datasync.ObjectMetadata|string Specifies whether you want DataSync to PRESERVE object metadata (default behavior) when transferring between object storage systems. If you want your DataSync task to ignore object metadata, specify the NONE value.

---@alias aws.datasync.OutputTagList aws.datasync.TagListEntry[]

