---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationAzureBlobRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the ARN of the Azure Blob Storage transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.AzureBlobSubdirectory Specifies path segments if you want to limit your transfer to a virtual directory in your container (for example, /my/images).
---@field AuthenticationType? aws.datasync.AzureBlobAuthenticationType|string Specifies the authentication method DataSync uses to access your Azure Blob Storage. DataSync can access blob storage using a shared access signature (SAS) or an OpenID Connect (OIDC) token.
---@field SasConfiguration? aws.datasync.AzureBlobSasConfiguration Specifies the SAS configuration that allows DataSync to access your Azure Blob Storage.
---@field FederatedIdentity? aws.datasync.AzureFederatedIdentityConfig Specifies the federated identity configuration that allows DataSync to access your Azure Blob Storage using an OpenID Connect (OIDC) token instead of a shared access signature (SAS). Provide either FederatedIdentity or SasConfiguration, but not both.
---@field BlobType? aws.datasync.AzureBlobType|string Specifies the type of blob that you want your objects or files to be when transferring them into Azure Blob Storage. Currently, DataSync only supports moving data into Azure Blob Storage as block blobs. For more information on blob types, see the Azure Blob Storage documentation.
---@field AccessTier? aws.datasync.AzureAccessTier|string Specifies the access tier that you want your objects or files transferred into. This only applies when using the location as a transfer destination. For more information, see Access tiers.
---@field AgentArns? aws.datasync.AgentArnList (Optional) Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the DataSync agent that can connect with your Azure Blob Storage container. If you are setting up an agentless cross-cloud transfer, you do not need to specify a value for this parameter.
---@field CmkSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CmkSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a DataSync-managed secret, such as an authentication token or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed KMS key.
---@field CustomSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CustomSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a customer-managed secret, such as an authentication token or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that provides access to the secret.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationAzureBlobResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationEfsRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon EFS transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.EfsSubdirectory Specifies a mount path for your Amazon EFS file system. This is where DataSync reads or writes data on your file system (depending on if this is a source or destination location).
---@field AccessPointArn? aws.datasync.UpdatedEfsAccessPointArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the access point that DataSync uses to mount your Amazon EFS file system.
---@field FileSystemAccessRoleArn? aws.datasync.UpdatedEfsIamRoleArn Specifies an Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that allows DataSync to access your Amazon EFS file system.
---@field InTransitEncryption? aws.datasync.EfsInTransitEncryption|string Specifies whether you want DataSync to use Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2 encryption when it transfers data to or from your Amazon EFS file system.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationEfsResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxLustreRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the FSx for Lustre transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.SmbSubdirectory Specifies a mount path for your FSx for Lustre file system. The path can include subdirectories.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxLustreResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxOntapRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the FSx for ONTAP transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Protocol? aws.datasync.FsxUpdateProtocol Specifies the data transfer protocol that DataSync uses to access your Amazon FSx file system.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.FsxOntapSubdirectory Specifies a path to the file share in the storage virtual machine (SVM) where you want to transfer data to or from.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxOntapResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxOpenZfsRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the FSx for OpenZFS transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Protocol? aws.datasync.FsxProtocol
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.SmbSubdirectory Specifies a subdirectory in the location's path that must begin with /fsx. DataSync uses this subdirectory to read or write data (depending on whether the file system is a source or destination location).

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxOpenZfsResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxWindowsRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the ARN of the FSx for Windows File Server transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.FsxWindowsSubdirectory Specifies a mount path for your file system using forward slashes. DataSync uses this subdirectory to read or write data (depending on whether the file system is a source or destination location).
---@field Domain? aws.datasync.UpdateSmbDomain Specifies the name of the Windows domain that your FSx for Windows File Server file system belongs to.
---@field User? aws.datasync.SmbUser Specifies the user with the permissions to mount and access the files, folders, and file metadata in your FSx for Windows File Server file system.
---@field Password? aws.datasync.SmbPassword|distilled.Secret Specifies the password of the user with the permissions to mount and access the files, folders, and file metadata in your FSx for Windows File Server file system.
---@field CmkSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CmkSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a DataSync-managed secret, such as a Password or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed KMS key.
---@field CustomSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CustomSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a customer-managed secret, such as a Password or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that provides access to the secret.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationFsxWindowsResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationHdfsRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the source HDFS cluster location.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.HdfsSubdirectory A subdirectory in the HDFS cluster. This subdirectory is used to read data from or write data to the HDFS cluster.
---@field NameNodes? aws.datasync.HdfsNameNodeList The NameNode that manages the HDFS namespace. The NameNode performs operations such as opening, closing, and renaming files and directories. The NameNode contains the information to map blocks of data to the DataNodes.
---@field BlockSize? aws.datasync.HdfsBlockSize The size of the data blocks to write into the HDFS cluster.
---@field ReplicationFactor? aws.datasync.HdfsReplicationFactor The number of DataNodes to replicate the data to when writing to the HDFS cluster.
---@field KmsKeyProviderUri? aws.datasync.KmsKeyProviderUri The URI of the HDFS cluster's Key Management Server (KMS).
---@field QopConfiguration? aws.datasync.QopConfiguration The Quality of Protection (QOP) configuration specifies the Remote Procedure Call (RPC) and data transfer privacy settings configured on the Hadoop Distributed File System (HDFS) cluster.
---@field AuthenticationType? aws.datasync.HdfsAuthenticationType|string The type of authentication used to determine the identity of the user.
---@field SimpleUser? aws.datasync.HdfsUser The user name used to identify the client on the host operating system.
---@field KerberosPrincipal? aws.datasync.KerberosPrincipal The Kerberos principal with access to the files and folders on the HDFS cluster.
---@field KerberosKeytab? aws.datasync.KerberosKeytabFile The Kerberos key table (keytab) that contains mappings between the defined Kerberos principal and the encrypted keys. You can load the keytab from a file by providing the file's address.
---@field KerberosKrb5Conf? aws.datasync.KerberosKrb5ConfFile The krb5.conf file that contains the Kerberos configuration information. You can load the krb5.conf file by providing the file's address. If you're using the CLI, it performs the base64 encoding for you. Otherwise, provide the base64-encoded text.
---@field AgentArns? aws.datasync.AgentArnList The Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the DataSync agents that can connect to your HDFS cluster.
---@field CmkSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CmkSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a DataSync-managed secret, such as a KerberosKeytab or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed KMS key.
---@field CustomSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CustomSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a customer-managed secret, such as a KerberosKeytab or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that provides access to the secret.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationHdfsResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationNfsRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the NFS transfer location that you want to update.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.NfsSubdirectory Specifies the export path in your NFS file server that you want DataSync to mount.
---@field ServerHostname? aws.datasync.ServerHostname Specifies the DNS name or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6) of the NFS file server that your DataSync agent connects to.
---@field OnPremConfig? aws.datasync.OnPremConfig
---@field MountOptions? aws.datasync.NfsMountOptions

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationNfsResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationObjectStorageRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the ARN of the object storage system location that you're updating.
---@field ServerPort? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageServerPort Specifies the port that your object storage server accepts inbound network traffic on (for example, port 443).
---@field ServerProtocol? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageServerProtocol|string Specifies the protocol that your object storage server uses to communicate.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.S3Subdirectory Specifies the object prefix for your object storage server. If this is a source location, DataSync only copies objects with this prefix. If this is a destination location, DataSync writes all objects with this prefix.
---@field ServerHostname? aws.datasync.ServerHostname Specifies the domain name or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6) of the object storage server that your DataSync agent connects to.
---@field AccessKey? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageAccessKey Specifies the access key (for example, a user name) if credentials are required to authenticate with the object storage server.
---@field SecretKey? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageSecretKey|distilled.Secret Specifies the secret key (for example, a password) if credentials are required to authenticate with the object storage server.
---@field FederatedIdentity? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageFederatedIdentityConfig Specifies the federated identity configuration that allows DataSync to access your object storage using an OpenID Connect (OIDC) token instead of a long-term access key and secret key. Provide either FederatedIdentity or the AccessKey/SecretKey credentials, but not both.
---@field AgentArns? aws.datasync.AgentArnList (Optional) Specifies the Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the DataSync agents that can connect with your object storage system. If you are setting up an agentless cross-cloud transfer, you do not need to specify a value for this parameter.
---@field ServerCertificate? aws.datasync.ObjectStorageCertificate Specifies a certificate chain for DataSync to authenticate with your object storage system if the system uses a private or self-signed certificate authority (CA). You must specify a single .pem file with a full certificate chain (for example, file:///home/user/.ssh/object_storage_certificates.pem).
---@field CmkSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CmkSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a DataSync-managed secret, such as an authentication token or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed KMS key.
---@field CustomSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CustomSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a customer-managed secret, such as an authentication token or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that provides access to the secret.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationObjectStorageResponse

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationS3Request
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon S3 transfer location that you're updating.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.S3Subdirectory Specifies a prefix in the S3 bucket that DataSync reads from or writes to (depending on whether the bucket is a source or destination location).
---@field S3StorageClass? aws.datasync.S3StorageClass|string Specifies the storage class that you want your objects to use when Amazon S3 is a transfer destination.
---@field S3Config? aws.datasync.S3Config

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationS3Response

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationSmbRequest
---@field LocationArn aws.datasync.LocationArn Specifies the ARN of the SMB location that you want to update.
---@field Subdirectory? aws.datasync.SmbSubdirectory Specifies the name of the share exported by your SMB file server where DataSync will read or write data. You can include a subdirectory in the share path (for example, /path/to/subdirectory). Make sure that other SMB clients in your network can also mount this path.
---@field ServerHostname? aws.datasync.ServerHostname Specifies the domain name or IP address (IPv4 or IPv6) of the SMB file server that your DataSync agent connects to.
---@field User? aws.datasync.SmbUser Specifies the user name that can mount your SMB file server and has permission to access the files and folders involved in your transfer. This parameter applies only if AuthenticationType is set to NTLM.
---@field Domain? aws.datasync.SmbDomain Specifies the Windows domain name that your SMB file server belongs to. This parameter applies only if AuthenticationType is set to NTLM.
---@field Password? aws.datasync.SmbPassword|distilled.Secret Specifies the password of the user who can mount your SMB file server and has permission to access the files and folders involved in your transfer. This parameter applies only if AuthenticationType is set to NTLM.
---@field CmkSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CmkSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a DataSync-managed secret, such as a Password or KerberosKeytab or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed KMS key.
---@field CustomSecretConfig? aws.datasync.CustomSecretConfig Specifies configuration information for a customer-managed secret, such as a Password or KerberosKeytab or set of credentials that DataSync uses to access a specific transfer location, and a customer-managed Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that provides access to the secret.
---@field AgentArns? aws.datasync.AgentArnList Specifies the DataSync agent (or agents) that can connect to your SMB file server. You specify an agent by using its Amazon Resource Name (ARN).
---@field MountOptions? aws.datasync.SmbMountOptions
---@field AuthenticationType? aws.datasync.SmbAuthenticationType|string Specifies the authentication protocol that DataSync uses to connect to your SMB file server. DataSync supports NTLM (default) and KERBEROS authentication.
---@field DnsIpAddresses? aws.datasync.DnsIpList Specifies the IP addresses (IPv4 or IPv6) for the DNS servers that your SMB file server belongs to. This parameter applies only if AuthenticationType is set to KERBEROS.
---@field KerberosPrincipal? aws.datasync.KerberosPrincipal Specifies a Kerberos prinicpal, which is an identity in your Kerberos realm that has permission to access the files, folders, and file metadata in your SMB file server.
---@field KerberosKeytab? aws.datasync.KerberosKeytabFile Specifies your Kerberos key table (keytab) file, which includes mappings between your Kerberos principal and encryption keys.
---@field KerberosKrb5Conf? aws.datasync.KerberosKrb5ConfFile Specifies a Kerberos configuration file (krb5.conf) that defines your Kerberos realm configuration.

---@class aws.datasync.UpdateLocationSmbResponse

---@alias aws.datasync.UpdateSmbDomain string

